.TH KTX_ENCODE 1 "2026-10-27" "ktx (Rust port)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktx_encode \- encode a KTX2 file to a block compressed format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktx
encode [OPTION...] <input\-file> <output\-file>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Encodes an uncompressed KTX2 file to ASTC
.RB ( \-\-format )
or to Basis Universal Basis\-LZ, UASTC or UASTC HDR
.RB ( \-\-codec ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-format <vkformat>
ASTC target format.
.TP
.B \-\-codec <codec>
basis\-lz, uastc, uastc\-hdr\-4x4 or uastc\-hdr\-6x6i.
.TP
.B \-\-astc\-quality, \-\-clevel, \-\-qlevel, \-\-uastc\-quality, \-\-uastc\-rdo
Encoder quality and rate\-distortion settings.
.TP
.B \-\-compare\-ssim, \-\-compare\-psnr
Report the encoding error.
.TP
.B \-\-zstd <level>, \-\-zlib <level>
Supercompress the result.
.TP
.B \-\-threads <n>
Number of encoder threads.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
ktx encode \-\-codec basis\-lz \-\-qlevel 200 in.ktx2 out.ktx2
.fi
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX\-Software (libktx and the ktx CLI); it is not
the Khronos build of the tool. The complete, current option list is printed by
.B ktx encode \-\-help.
.SH SEE ALSO
ktx(1)
